{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792367356,"nonce":"SX3E02E0VXAS8ZIIllpZJqyOBes=","message":"Gradients with stops, spreads and conic are in e306b93b (local). GpuPrimitive gets gradient_table (a pointer into aux_data to the stop table, zero for none, so the two-stop fast path and every existing primitive are unchanged; the struct is now 30 vec4 with the side colours), FillType gets ConicGradient, and sdf_core with its vb and dt variants read the table as blinc_ts does, mixing in premultiplied colour (the fwidth shortcut for a sub-pixel period became a fixed epsilon, since a derivative in non-uniform control flow does not validate). The decoder reads the producer's three forms (a middle stop, other first and last offsets, a table in the list's tail) and a plan Run carries the tables its primitives name, rebased when runs merge. Checked on a real device against a CPU evaluation of the ABI's formulas, over eight gradients (three and five stops, other offsets, repeat, reflect radial, radial with stops, conic with two and five stops), worst error 1 of 255 over about 6000 pixels each, and by mutation (a broken repeat fold fails by 221). Risk to watch: the stop loop adds a while loop and aux reads to sdf_core's fragment shader, and the split pipelines exist because the monolithic shader did not compile on the PowerVR GPU in the notes; this has only been compiled here (Metal), not on that hardware. Remaining: mask, backdrop, canvases, local clip, clip-path frame, fade rect, notch.","files":null}]}